As-per the Discourse discussion here: https://discourse.bokeh.org/t/flatpickr-date-display-format/6630

Currently,  we are constrained to the ISO yyyy-mm-dd format for the flatpickr implementation of DatePicker (post-2.0);

![image](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/7271339/97622498-c0acca80-19fa-11eb-97a3-20911adc49ae.png)

It would be great to expose the existing flatpickr dateFormat options to the user, retaining the standard ISO display as a default.

Looks like flatpickr supports everything from the JS side already via their config.dateFormat options;

https://flatpickr.js.org/formatting/

- [x] issues: fixes #12767 
- [x] release document entry (if new feature or API change)

@mattpap there was an old "datepicker" ref that was broken, not sure why docs built in the old PR to be honest. As long as that is updated, can you confirm whether the list of widgets that can have tooltips is still accurate (do the new pickers also support?)
